@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: Mixed MVP / future. Retained broader-product associations require explicit future node labels; MVP uses only core/basic ProjectForge.
title AFTER MVP — advanced model — Proposed LC-06 work views and coherent Sprint Backlog
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

class WorkProject {
 projectId / lifecycle / version
}
class Board {
 column-to-state mapping / version
}
class CardPlacement {
 explicit item or task target
 position / version
}
class BacklogItem <<After_MVP>> {
 criteria / work state / version
 acceptance provenance
}
class Task {
 parent context / work state
 assignment / version
}
class SprintBacklog <<After_MVP>> {
 Sprint Goal
 selected item identities
 delivery plan / version
}
class Sprint <<After_MVP>> {
 period / lifecycle / version
}
class SprintOutcomeRecord {
 historical goal / scope / plan context
 actual goal and item outcomes
}
WorkProject --> Board : configured work view
Board --> CardPlacement : presents
CardPlacement --> BacklogItem : item target
CardPlacement --> Task : task target
BacklogItem --> Task : reviewed task relationship
WorkProject --> BacklogItem : project work
WorkProject --> Sprint : planned period
Sprint --> SprintBacklog : one coherent plan
SprintBacklog --> BacklogItem : selected work
Sprint --> SprintOutcomeRecord : explicit period-end record
note bottom of CardPlacement
 Column position is not acceptance evidence.
 Views share authoritative work state.
end note
note bottom of SprintOutcomeRecord
 Period end is not goal achievement.
 Later edits do not rewrite recorded context.
 Cardinalities and disposition rules need review.
end note
@enduml
